/// @file reciprocal
/// @brief Explicit reciprocal division for 32-bit fixed-point types.
///
/// Strategies trade accuracy, execution time and ROM table size without
/// changing gba::fixed::operator/. Call a strategy with a denominator to
/// prepare an owning divider, or with a numerator and denominator to divide:
///
/// @code{.cpp}
/// using q16 = gba::fixed<int, 16>;
/// constexpr auto divide = gba::reciprocal::normalized<8, 2>;
/// auto quotient = divide(q16{12}, q16{3});
/// auto depth = divide(q16{3});
/// auto x = depth(q16{12});
/// auto y = depth(q16{8});
/// @endcode
///
/// @section reciprocal_strategies Strategies
///
/// - normalized uses a midpoint seed table and Newton-Raphson refinement.
/// - affine uses a straight-line seed and refinement without a table.
/// - direct uses a table for bounded integer denominator magnitudes.
/// - corrected wraps a supported strategy for exact truncating results.
///
/// Each strategy exposes table_bytes. Matching configurations share immutable
/// tables in ROM; copying a strategy does not copy its table.
///
/// @section reciprocal_ranges Batch calls and preconditions
///
/// Strategies accept (numerators, denominators, out); prepared dividers accept
/// (numerators, out). Ranges must be contiguous, sized and equal in length,
/// with matching fixed-point element types and writable output. Direct batch
/// denominators use 32-bit integers. Batch results match scalar calls.
///
/// Denominators must be nonzero and quotients must fit the result type.
/// Unsigned results cannot represent negative nonzero quotients. Violations
/// assert in debug builds, trap in release builds and fail constant evaluation.
/// Prepared dividers retain no references to their original denominators.
///
/// All call forms support constant evaluation with matching runtime results.
/// Runtime arithmetic executes ARM code in IWRAM; batching amortises kernel
/// call overhead. Strategies do not change the CPU mode or WAITCNT.
///
/// @see gba::reciprocal::normalized_strategy
/// @see gba::reciprocal::affine_strategy
/// @see gba::reciprocal::direct_strategy
/// @see gba::reciprocal::corrected_strategy
#pragma once

#include <gba/bits/reciprocal/affine.hpp>
#include <gba/bits/reciprocal/corrected.hpp>
#include <gba/bits/reciprocal/direct.hpp>
#include <gba/bits/reciprocal/normalized.hpp>
